          "id": 1808109353,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ah, I only tested with the interface list which shows up in the main window before making/opening a capture.  That one does start working correctly with this change.\n\nBefore this change, it would always default to showing all available interfaces when Wireshark is launched, irrespective of what had previously been chosen in the dropdown menu above and to the right of the interface list.\n\nWith this change, it now remembers whether or not you chose to show all interfaces in the dropdown menu, and that setting correctly takes effect upon relaunching Wireshark.\n\nI haven't delved into the **Manage Interfaces** dialog code at all, but would changing [the line you suggested](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/ui/qt/manage_interfaces_dialog.cpp#L195) make it impossible to un-hide interfaces which had previously been hidden?  Filtering seems undesirable in that context... but perhaps I misunderstand it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f4a609abaf984c9cfe277f1321b8db104aea7290fcbb7fb0c5749a00d32e39?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dariusd0"
          },
